Strongest Password-Given a string password, determine the minimum number of steps required to make it a strong password.
A password is considered strong if: Its length is between 6 and 20 characters, inclusive.
It contains at least one lowercase English letter.
It contains at least one uppercase English letter.
It contains at least one digit.
It does not contain three or more consecutive identical characters.
In one step, you can insert, delete, or replace one character.
Return the minimum number of steps required to make the password strong.
Examples-Input: "a" ; Output: 5, Because the password needs at least 6 characters and is missing uppercase and digit types.
